/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A helper stores one of its arguments into another. Cast inside a rabbit, with the row made there and the container outside.

    What a function stores into what it is given is written down as it is checked, and judged at each
    cast, where both depths are known. This was accepted: inside the helper both are parameters, at depth 0. (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O4). */

Bind void to tuck, given (the series of series of number bag, the series of number row):
    Insert row into bag.
Done.
Define keeper as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define row as a series of number with (1, 2).
    Cast tuck on (keeper, row).
Done.
State keeper.
